{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1504423-theory-liminal-exalted-will-be-given-the-terrestrial-keyword-for-martial-arts","id":1504423,"title":"Theory: Liminal Exalted will be given the Terrestrial keyword for Martial Arts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-05T07:32:25-08:00","id":1504423,"title":"Theory: Liminal Exalted will be given the Terrestrial keyword for Martial Arts","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">In 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition, Martial Arts styles were separated into three tiers: Terrestrial, Celestial, and Sidereal.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">3<sup>rd</sup> Edition changed this system by making all Martial Arts styles available to all Exalted and modifying how much power each type of Exalted could gain from each Martial Arts Charm based on keywords. This is roughly analogous to the tiers of power seen in 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">The <b>Terrestrial</b> keyword means that Dragon Blooded gain a lesser effect when using the Martial Arts Charm, while the <b>Mastery</b> keyword means that Solar, Abyssal, and Sidereal Exalted gain a greater effect.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">We know that Lunar Exalted use Martial Arts Charm unmodified by either keyword. If 3<sup>rd</sup> Edition follows the pattern established in 2<sup>nd</sup> Edition, it is reasonable to assume that Infernal and Alchemical Exalted will also use Martial Arts Charms unmodified by keywords.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">So, where does that leave the Liminal Exalted? I believe that the Liminal Exalted will be assigned the <b>Terrestrial</b> keyword.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">Let\u2019s review the evidence.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>Exhibit A</b>: On pg.286 in <i>Dragon Blooded: What Fire Has Wrought</i>, we have this line describing who can learn Immaculate Martial Arts.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><i>\u201c<span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">The Immaculate styles are intensely demanding. While anyone can learn the fundamentals of the styles, their Charms can only be learned by the Dragon-Blooded and by other martial artists that aren\u2019t restricted by the </span></i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Terrestrial</span></i></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> keyword, such as Solars and Sidereals.\u201d</span></i></span></span></i></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">When I first read this, I was confused. Dragon Blooded are the </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">only</span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> Exalted who are restricted by the </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Terrestrial</span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> keyword (</span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Exalted 3<sup>rd</sup> Edition Core</span></i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">, Pg. 427). Why bother including a line about a restriction that effectively restricts no one?</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">I thought that perhaps this meant that Immaculate Martial Arts couldn\u2019t be learned by mortals. Again, it turns out this was a restriction that was already established. </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><b><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Exhibit B</span></b></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">: Pg. 426 in </span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">3<sup>rd</sup> Edition Core</span></i></span></span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"> states:</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2-Roman\"><span style=\"color:black\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">\u201cThe Charms of a style are organized into a single tree, which can be learned by any of the Exalted (and certain other powerful supernatural beings).\u201d</span></i></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">So, we\u2019ve established that:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">1. Only Exalted and other beings of similar power can learn the Charms of supernatural Martial Arts.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">2. Furthermore, the Immaculate Styles can only be learned by the Dragon Blooded and Exalted not restricted by the <b>Terrestrial</b> keyword.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">3. The restriction mentioned in point 2 applies to no currently published type of Exalted.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">4. There are two distinct types of Exalted that are as-yet unpublished (Liminal and Getimian).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><span style=\"color:black\">Therefore, I postulate that the Liminal Exalted will be given the <b>Terrestrial</b> keyword when their books are published.</span></span><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T10:22:29-08:00","id":1504454,"title":"","content":"For some more supporting evidence: there's also the Terrestrial Keyword in Essence, which explicitly includes the Liminal Exalted as part of that category.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T11:27:33-08:00","id":1504469,"title":"","content":"Also, most Exigents are on the same kind of assumed area of play as Dragon-Blooded and Liminals and also have the Terrestrial keyword applied to their Charms. The Strawmaiden is more Lunar-ish since she's not really either way on Martial Arts. The Puppetteer and Sovereigns are explicilty Terrestrial playstle and deal with it. Architects deal with it by default, but can give up one of their Foundaiton Attributes to become like Lunars and the Strawmaiden.<br /> <br /> In general the thing with Martial Arts and Artiffacts for Terrestirals appears to be that they suffer the Terrestrial keyword, while being neutral in their main magical material and Dissonant with the rest. Celestial play Exalts usually are Martial Arts neutral, Resonant with their main material and neutrla with the rest unless thematic (Strawmaiden is Dissonant with soulsteel, Sidereals and Getimians wiht non-starmetal). Dragon-Blooded stand-out as an exception to this but are noted as explicitly meant to be pretty notably good with artifacts in their themes due to heirlooms ands tuff.<br /> <br /> This all being said, expect Liminals, stated many times by devs as more for Terrestrial arenas of play, to deal with Terrestrial in Martial Arts. Not we already know their material resonance too: neutral with souslteel, Dissonant with everything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T11:33:43-08:00","id":1504470,"title":"","content":"Oh, as an aside, at this time it's noted Infernals will likely have Mastery since nothing really is about them that makes it so they shouldn't this time around. They can learn Sidereal styles like Abyssals and Solars, and in general there isn't some diagetic reason tehir powers (whicha re sitll their own not literal Yozi ones) shouldn't be able to wield such stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T14:11:36-08:00","id":1504643,"title":"","content":"Also, while we are on the subject, I have mixed feelings about Exalted (and creatures of similar power) being the only ones capable of learning supernatural martial arts. Like come on: mortals and the [X]-blooded have a hard enough time as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>What do we want? 3rd Edition Sidereals!<br /> When do we want it? In accordance with the dictates of Fate!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/867-jimborg","name":"Jimborg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-06T15:08:51-08:00","id":1504653,"title":"","content":"Mortals who learn supernatural martial arts aren't quite mortal anymore. There's actually an example of thisin <i>Adversaries of the Righteous</i>, a leader of a Snake Style dojo who has snake powers. The big thing relaly is the system barely supports mortals as-is, and having mortals with soemthing that's basically Snake Style Charms but like, a spirit is in them or drugs, is fine. It's just not something that's really served by trying to shoehorn into what amounts to extended prelude mechanics. Most mortals encountered are QCs or important NPCs that if they need the fighitng prowess, should just have it wihtout worrying that it's not represented by the rules PCs are built on.<br /> <br /> Same goes with god-bloods. Some might. Many are not even relaly more than like, dudes wiht some Merits or a Charm or two. Some might be powerful enough to learn lots of Charms. Again, they're kind of more bespke this edition than in previous ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}